{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":7,"query":"name=Klein&limit=10&title=Abundance","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":[{"@version":"3.8","titleInfo":{"title":"Peter Bruegel the Elder, artist of abundance","subTitle":"an illustrated portrait of his life, era, and art"},"name":[{"@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Klein, H. Arthur","role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Klein, Mina C."},{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Klein, Mina C.,","role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"author"}}}],"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"biography"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Literature"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Biographies"},{"@authority":"lcgft","#text":"Literature"}],"originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York"}}],"dateIssued":[{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"1968"},[1968]],"issuance":"monographic","agent":{"namePart":"Macmillan"}},"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":[{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"xix, 188 p., [8] p. of plates illus. (part col.) 26 cm."},{"form":{"@type":"Illustrative content","#text":"illustration"}},{"form":{"@type":"Color content","#text":"polychrome"}}],"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"Describes the life and world of Pieter Bruegel, concentrating on his works and influence on Western art."},"tableOfContents":{"@type":"Contents","#text":"The quiet apprentice at the Print Shop of the Four Winds -- Bruegel's antwerp: city at the Crossroads of the world -- Certainties and uncertainties about names, places, and dates -- An education in art -- A new artist amidst engravers -- His own, his native land -- From Flemish lowlands to mountain peaks--the great journey begins -- Sights of ships and the sea in Italy -- Rome--and the Tower of Babel -- From mountain lands to landscape engravings -- Into landscapes of the human heart -- Further follies and difficult virtues -- Paintings of multiplicity and darker moods -- Marriage and a new look at life -- The splendid \"seasons\" and wedding celebrations -- Masterworks from troubled times -- Final triumphs."},"note":{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"by H. Arthur Klein & Mina C. Klein."},"subject":[{"geographicCode":{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"e-be---"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Bruegel, Pieter,",{"@type":"date","#text":"approximately 1525-1569"}]}},{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Bruegel, Pieter,",{"@type":"date","#text":"approximately 1525-1569"}]},"genre":"Juvenile literature"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Painters","genre":"Biography"}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"ND673.B73 K42"},{"@authority":"ddc","#text":"760/.0924"}],"relatedItem":[{"@type":"otherFormat","@otherType":"Online version:","@displayLabel":"Online version:","titleInfo":{"title":"Peter Bruegel the Elder, artist of abundance"},"originInfo":{"publisher":"New York, Macmillan [1968]"},"identifier":{"@type":"local","#text":"(OCoLC)691127800"},"name":{"namePart":"Klein, H. Arthur."}},{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990025084960203941/catalog"}}],"identifier":[{"@type":"lccn","#text":"^^^68020616^//r84"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"441561"}],"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/0000000109432246","#text":"Fine Arts Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"FA4066.1.1006"},null,null],"extension":[{"librarycloud":{"HarvardRepositories":{"HarvardRepository":"Fine Arts"},"originalDocument":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/harvard.librarycloud.marc/990025084960203941","priorrecordids":{"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALEPH","#text":"002508496"}},"processingDate":"2026-08-31T04:18Z"}},{"sets":null}],"recordInfo":{"recordContentSource":{"@authority":"marcorg"},"recordCreationDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"920513"},"recordChangeDate":{"@encoding":"iso8601","#text":"20020606"},"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALMA","#text":"990025084960203941"},"recordOrigin":"Converted from MARCXML to MODS version 3.8 using\n\t\t\t\t\tMARC21slim_MODS3-8_XSL2-0.xsl (Revision 2.79 2025/03/28)"}},{"@version":"3.8","titleInfo":{"title":"Abundance ","subTitle":"What progress takes"},"name":[{"@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Klein, Ezra","role":[{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}},{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"author"}}]},{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Klein, Ezra"}],"typeOfResource":"sound recording-nonmusical","genre":[{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"spoken word"},{"@authority":"local","#text":"Electronic books."}],"originInfo":[{"place":{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},"dateIssued":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2025"},"issuance":"monographic","edition":"Unabridged."},{"@eventType":"publication","place":{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York :"}},"agent":{"namePart":"Simon and Schuster Audio,","role":{"roleTerm":"publisher"}},"dateIssued":"2025."}],"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":[{"form":[{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"electronic"},{"@authority":"marccategory","#text":"electronic resource"},{"@authority":"marcsmd","#text":"remote"},{"@authority":"marccategory","#text":"sound recording"},{"@type":"media","@authority":"rdamedia","#text":"audio"},{"@type":"media","@authority":"rdamedia","#text":"computer"},{"@type":"carrier","@authority":"rdacarrier","#text":"online resource"}],"extent":"1 online resource (13 audio files) : digital"},{"form":[{"@type":"Type of recording","#text":"digital"},{"@type":"Configuration of playback channels","#text":"stereo"}]}],"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"#1 NEW YORK TIMES BESTSELLER ONE OF BARACK OBAMA'S FAVORITE BOOKS OF 2025 andbull; NEW YORK TIMES 100 NOTABLE BOOKS OF 2025 KIRKUS REVIEWS BEST BOOKS OF 2025 NPR BOOKS WE LOVE 2025 \"A must-read for progressives who want a blueprint for reforming government so it can deliver for working people.\" -Barack Obama \"A terrific book...Powerful and persuasive.\" -Fareed Zakaria \"Spectacular...Offers a comprehensive indictment of the current problems and a clear path forward...Klein and Thompson usher in a mood shift. They inspire hope and enlarge the imagination.\" -David Brooks, The New York Times From bestselling authors and journalistic titans Ezra Klein and Derek Thompson, Abundance is a once-in-a-generation, paradigm-shifting call to renew a politics of plenty, face up to the failures of liberal governance, and abandon the chosen scarcities that have deformed American life. To trace the history of the twenty-first century so far is to trace a history of unaffordability and shortage. After years of refusing to build sufficient housing, America has a national housing crisis. After years of limiting immigration, we don't have enough workers. Despite decades of being warned about the consequences of climate change, we haven't built anything close to the clean-energy infrastructure we need. Ambitious public projects are finished late and over budget-if they are ever finished at all. The crisis that's clicking into focus now has been building for decades-because we haven't been building enough. Abundance explains that our problems today are not the results of yesteryear's villains. Rather, one generation's solutions have become the next gener­ation's problems. Rules and regulations designed to solve the problems of the 1970s often prevent urban-density and green-energy projects that would help solve the problems of the 2020s. Laws meant to ensure that government considers the consequences of its actions have made it too difficult for government to act consequentially. In the last few decades, our capacity to see problems has sharpened while our ability to solve them has diminished. Progress requires facing up to the institutions in life that are not working as they need to. It means, for liberals, recognizing when the government is failing. It means, for conservatives, recognizing when the government is needed. In a book exploring how we can move from a liberalism that not only protects and pre­serves but also builds , Klein and Thompson trace the political, economic, and cultural barriers to progress and propose a path toward a politics of abundance. At a time when movements of scarcity are gaining power in country after country, this is an answer that meets the challenges of the moment while grappling honestly with the fury so many rightfully feel."},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Ezra Klein."},"Unabridged.",{"@type":"performers","#text":"Narrator: Ezra Klein."},{"@type":"system details","#text":"Requires the Libby app or a modern web browser."}],"subject":[{"@authority":"OverDrive","topic":"Nonfiction"},{"@authority":"OverDrive","topic":"Business"},{"@authority":"OverDrive","topic":"Politics"}],"classification":{"@authority":"bisacsh","#text":"BUS069000 POL028000 POL040000"},"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9781797168609"},{"@type":"stock number","#text":"631BB847-6A45-4B02-A0E3-2CB1CD3928C2 OverDrive, Inc."}],"relatedItem":{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/99161563197003941/catalog"}},"location":[null,null],"extension":[{"librarycloud":{"originalDocument":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/harvard.librarycloud.marc/99161563197003941","processingDate":"2026-05-11T04:15Z"}},{"sets":null}],"recordInfo":{"desc